BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 671.00 Td (Appreciate you reading this newsletter, I hope the content and resources are helping you level up as an) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 657.60 Td (engineer. If you want me to write about something specific, just message me or comment on the post.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 637.70 Td (Note: This article on was originally published on my blog -) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 624.30 Td (https://pradyumnachippigiri.dev/blogs/rag-systems-part1) Tj ET
BT /F2 10.5 Tf 58.00 593.40 Td (What is RAG?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 575.75 Td (RAG stands for Retrieval Augmented Generation. It was introduced in the paper Retrieval-Augmented) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 562.35 Td (Generation for Knowledge-Intensive NLP Tasks.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 542.45 Td (Each step can be roughly broken down to:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 522.55 Td (Retrieval \226 Seeking relevant information from a source given a query. For example, getting relevant passages of) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 509.15 Td (Wikipedia text from a database given a question.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 489.25 Td (Augmented \226 Using the relevant retrieved information to modify an input to a generative model \(e.g., an LLM\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 469.35 Td (Generation \226 Generating an output given an input. For example, in the case of an LLM, generating a passage of) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 455.95 Td (text given an input prompt.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 436.05 Td (Thanks for reading LevelYouUp! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 416.15 Td (You can think of RAG like an open-book exam:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 396.25 Td (You or your mind is the LLM.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 376.35 Td (The textbook is your external knowledge base \(PDFs, docs, webpages\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 356.45 Td (When a question is asked, you don\222t memorize the entire book, instead, you first flip through the index/table of) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 343.05 Td (contents to find the most relevant pages -> This \223flipping and finding the right pages\224 is Retrieval.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 323.15 Td (Once you have the right pages open, you read them and augment your understanding with that information ->) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 309.75 Td (This is Augmentation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 289.85 Td (Finally, based on the question + the retrieved pages, you think, synthesize, and produce a well-structured) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 276.45 Td (answer -> This is Generation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 256.55 Td (So the pipeline is:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 236.65 Td (Index search -> retrieve relevant pages -> read them -> think -> answer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 216.75 Td (Exactly how RAG works:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 196.85 Td (Retriever: finds relevant chunks like an exam index) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 176.95 Td (Augmentor: inserts those chunks into the model\222s prompt) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 157.05 Td (LLM Generator: reasons using the question + retrieved context) Tj ET
