q 479.00 0 0 245.89 58.00 527.11 cm /Im3 Do Q
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 518.11 Td (You might now ask, our mind is not capable to read the entire book to answer quickly to the question, but LLMs) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 504.71 Td (can right, so what is the use of RAG ? I asked ChatGPT and Google Gemini to answer questions from a 1000) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 491.31 Td (page pdf and here\222s how it answered.) Tj ET
q 479.00 0 0 279.42 58.00 187.00 cm /Im4 Do Q
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 178.00 Td (As you can see that Chatgpt was not able to answer as its context window is lesser compared to Gemini. Hence,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 164.60 Td (Google Gemini was able to read and output the question asked. But, here comes the catch: Even though LLMs) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 151.20 Td (today have massive context windows and can technically \223read\224 huge amounts of text, there are three major) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 137.80 Td (limitations that make RAG still essential.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 117.90 Td (Even though LLMs today have massive context windows and can technically \223read\224 huge amounts of text, there) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 104.50 Td (are two major limitations that make RAG still essential. - Cost explodes with large context windows: LLMs charge) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 91.10 Td (per input + output token. Sending a 200K-token PDF into the model every time is insanely expensive.) Tj ET
