BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 676.25 Td (Step 1: Build a small, high-quality test dataset) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 656.35 Td (Before metrics, you need data:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 636.45 Td (Collect a set of questions your system should handle) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 616.55 Td (For each question, store:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 596.65 Td (Ground-truth answer) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 576.75 Td (Relevant source passages/document IDs) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 556.85 Td (Even 30\226100 good examples are enough to start. This becomes your RAG test set.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 536.95 Td (Step 2: Evaluate Retrieval \226 \223Did we fetch the right context?\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 517.05 Td (Before you judge the final answer, you want to know: \223Is my retriever even giving the model the right stuff to) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 503.65 Td (work with?\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 483.75 Td (So, for each question in the test set:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 463.85 Td (Run it through the retriever \(but don\222t call the LLM yet\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 443.95 Td (Collect the top-k chunks that come back.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 424.05 Td (Look at those chunks and ask:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 404.15 Td (If I were the model, could I answer this question from these chunks?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 384.25 Td (There are two ways to do this:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 364.35 Td (Manual check \(great in the early stages\): Skim a subset of questions and their retrieved chunks and judge them) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 350.95 Td (yourself:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 331.05 Td (\223Yes, this chunk clearly answers the question.\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 311.15 Td (\223No, this is just boilerplate/irrelevant.\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 291.25 Td (Automatic check \(LLM-as-judge\): Use another model to score relevance. For each \(question, chunk\) pair, you) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 277.85 Td (can ask: \223Given this question and this chunk, how relevant is this chunk to answering the question? Score from) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 264.45 Td (1 \(not relevant\) to 5 \(highly relevant\).\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 244.55 Td (This step isolates retrieval from generation:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 224.65 Td (If retrieval is weak, the LLM is basically guessing, no matter how good your prompt or model is.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 204.75 Td (If retrieval looks good but the final answers are still bad, that\222s a strong signal that the problem is in the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 191.35 Td (Generation step \(prompt design, model choice, or output constraints\), not in the retriever.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 171.45 Td (Step 3: Evaluate Generation \226 \223Is the answer grounded & correct?\224) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 151.55 Td (Now we plug in the LLM and evaluate the answers themselves.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 131.65 Td (For each question:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 111.75 Td (Run full RAG: query -> retrieval -> generation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 91.85 Td (Get the final answer.) Tj ET
