BT /F2 10.5 Tf 58.00 648.50 Td (What is Supabase?) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 630.85 Td (There are many products in this space, if you\222ve used Firebase or Appwrite, you already know the category:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 617.45 Td (BaaS \(Backend as a Service\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 597.55 Td (Thanks for reading LevelYouUp! Subscribe for free to receive new posts and support my work.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 577.65 Td (When you build your first few projects, you eventually start seeing a pattern: the same backend pieces keep) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 564.25 Td (repeating like auth, database, storage, user management, file handling, etc. Every app needs them, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 550.85 Td (rebuilding those from scratch each time is exhausting.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 530.95 Td (That\222s why tools like Firebase, Appwrite, and Supabase exist. They package these common backend building) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 517.55 Td (blocks into ready-to-use APIs, so you can focus on your frontend instead of spinning up servers, databases, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 504.15 Td (auth systems manually.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 484.25 Td (This means you can build an entire application in React or Next.js and directly interact with the BaaS no custom) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 470.85 Td (backend server needed for most use-cases.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 450.95 Td (So Supabase is one of these BaaS platforms, but it stands out because it\222s built on top of PostgreSQL, is) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 437.55 Td (open-source, and gives you an SQL-first developer experience. And it handles scale enormously well.) Tj ET
