BT /F2 19 Tf 58.00 772.00 Td (Distributed Data Parallelism) Tj ET
0.46 g
BT /F3 8.6 Tf 58.00 740.25 Td (2026-10-02 \267 ai) Tj ET
0 g
0.55 g
BT /F1 7.6 Tf 58.00 724.75 Td (Source: Engineering notes \227 pradyumnac26.github.io) Tj ET
0 g
0.84 g 58.00 703.05 479.00 0.70 re f
0 g
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 694.75 Td (Distributed Data Parallelism \(DDP\) is one of the strategy to Scale Neural Network Training Across Multiple) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 681.35 Td (GPUs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 661.45 Td (We saw the 2 problems in scaling neural networks in this post) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 641.55 Td (Distributed Data Parallelism solves scaling when data is the bottleneck,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 621.65 Td (The core idea is simple: we want to process larger batches of data by spreading the work across multiple GPUs.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 601.75 Td (In practice, replicate the entire neural network model on each GPU, split the data batch across GPUs, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 588.35 Td (synchronize gradients.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 568.45 Td (The steps go like this :) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 548.55 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 548.55 Td (Split the training dataset into batches.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 532.65 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 532.65 Td (Divide that batch data into equal shards \(one per GPU\). Each shard data is a subset of that particular batch) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 519.25 Td (data, together they cover the full batch.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 503.35 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 503.35 Td (Define one neural network \(architecture + initial weights\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 487.45 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 487.45 Td (Copy that neural network to every GPU so each has the same weights at the start of training) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 471.55 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 471.55 Td (Place each data shard on different GPUs \(Batch 0 -> GPU 0, Batch 1 -> GPU 1, \205\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 455.65 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 455.65 Td (All GPUs run forward pass at the same time on their respective shard data. Each gets its own loss /) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 442.25 Td (activations.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 426.35 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 426.35 Td (All GPUs run backward at the same time. Each computes local gradients from its shard \(different data ->) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 412.95 Td (usually different local grads\).) Tj ET
