BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 694.75 Td (ReLu is called as the Rectified Linear Unit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 674.85 Td (Just like Sigmoid activation function and Tanh activation function, ReLU takes the raw logit $z = wx+b$ and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 661.45 Td (transforms it into something else. But unlike those two, it doesn't squash anything into a bounded range.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 641.55 Td ($$ \\text{ReLU}\(z\) = \\max\(0, z\) $$) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 621.65 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 621.65 Td (if z < 0 : then output is 0) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 605.75 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 605.75 Td (elif z > 0 : output is z) Tj ET
q 479.00 0 0 301.77 58.00 283.08 cm /Im30 Do Q
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 274.08 Td (Since ReLU is defined piecewise, we differentiate each piece separately.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 254.18 Td (For $z < 0$: the function is just the constant $0$. The derivative of a constant is always $0$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 234.28 Td ($$ \\text{ReLU}'\(z\) = 0 \\quad \\text{for } z<0 $$) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 214.38 Td (For $z > 0$: the function is $\\text{ReLU}\(z\) = z$. The derivative of $z$ with respect to $z$ is $1$.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 194.48 Td ($$ \\text{ReLU}'\(z\) = 1 \\quad \\text{for } z>0 $$ at z = 0 Relu is not defined, and so derivative also will be) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 181.08 Td (undefined. Hence there will be a sharp jump from 0 to 1 in the derivative graph.) Tj ET
