q 479.00 0 0 310.29 58.00 462.71 cm /Im31 Do Q
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 453.71 Td (So the derivative is either 0, or 1. The advantages of this is that :) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 433.81 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 433.81 Td (There wont be any Vanishing Gradient effect.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 417.91 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 417.91 Td (So when backprop is happening we are multiplying repeatedly with 1s, so learning is faster as it descends) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 404.51 Td (quickly in the gradient descent process.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 72.00 388.61 Td (\225) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 388.61 Td (It is cheap to compute as computers are super fast at handling 0s and 1s, instead of computing $e^{-z}$ or) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 80.01 375.21 Td ($e^z$ for every neuron like how Tanh and Sigmoid does.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 359.31 Td (One drawback of this activation function is that :) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 339.41 Td (Once $z<0$ for everything, $\\text{ReLU}'\(z\) = 0$. Now look at the chain again:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 319.51 Td ($$ \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial w} = \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial a}\\cdot\\underbrace{\\frac{\\partial a}{\\partial) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 306.11 Td (z}}_{=\\,0}\\cdot\\frac{\\partial z}{\\partial w} = 0 $$) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 286.21 Td (The gradient itself is 0. So the weights never get updated, irrespective of the learning rate $\\eta$ . So learning) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 272.81 Td (never happens) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 252.91 Td ($$ w_{\\text{new}} = w_{\\text{old}} - \\eta \\times 0 = w_{\\text{old}} $$) Tj ET
BT /F2 12 Tf 58.00 220.01 Td (The clean summary of what you figured out) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 199.41 Td ($$ \\text{High } \\eta \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\text{large -ve } w \\;\\longrightarrow\\; z<0 \\text{ for all inputs}) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 186.01 Td (\\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\frac{\\partial a}{\\partial z}=0 \\;\\longrightarrow\\; \\frac{\\partial L}{\\partial w}=0 $$) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 166.11 Td (This problem is also called as the Dying Relu Problem. But with a proper setting of the learning rate this is less) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 152.71 Td (frequently an issue.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 132.81 Td (Thats why Leaky ReLu was introduced.) Tj ET
