BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 694.75 Td (The sigmoid function is basically just the inverse of Logits. The sigmoid function maps arbitrary real values back) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 681.35 Td (to the range [0, 1]. The larger the value, the closer to 1 you\222ll get.) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 661.45 Td (From the above, we can derive:) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 641.55 Td ($$ \\text{logit}\(p\) = \\log\\left\(\\frac{p}{1-p}\\right\) $$) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 621.65 Td ($$ e^{\\text{logit}} = \\frac{p}{1-p} $$) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 601.75 Td ($$ e^{-\\text{logit}} = \\frac{1-p}{p} $$) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 581.85 Td ($$ e^{-\\text{logit}} = \\frac{1}{p} - \\frac{p}{p} = \\frac{1}{p} - 1 $$) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 561.95 Td ($$ \\frac{1}{p} = 1 + e^{-\\text{logit}} $$) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 542.05 Td ($$ p = \\frac{1}{1 + e^{-\\text{logit}}} $$) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 522.15 Td ($$ p = \\sigma\(\\text{z}\) = \\sigma\(\\text{logit}\) = \\frac{1}{1+e^{-\\text{logit}}} = \\frac{1}{1+e^{-z}} $$) Tj ET
BT /F1 9.6 Tf 58.00 502.25 Td (where ?? is the sigmoid function.) Tj ET
